<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine 2-year note coupon falls to 11.625 pct.</title>
<headline>Philippine 2-year note coupon falls to 11.625 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield on the Philippine two-year treasury note fell to 11.625 percent from the previous month's 12.0 percent, the Bureau of Treasury said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The auction committee awarded 4.0 billion pesos out of the 6.635 billion pesos bid.</p>
<p>Accepted bids at the monthly auction ranged from 11.00 to 11.70 percent with an average of 11.47 percent. A month ago, accepted bids ranged from 11.6 to 12.0 percent.</p>
<p>Traders had expected a fall in the coupon after Monday's drop in Treasury bill rates.</p>
<p>-- Manila Newsroom (63 2) 841-8914 Fax 817-6267</p>
</text>
